# Laptop-only packages.
#
# Applied after the shared Brewfile by scripts/init.sh, which picks this file from
# scripts/host-profile.sh. The split is by machine, not by GUI vs CLI: the Mac mini is
# used interactively too, so anything that is not machine-specific stays in Brewfile.

# Tailscale, as the GUI app rather than the formula the Mac mini gets. The menu bar is
# worth having on the machine that is driven by hand, and the laptop has no reason to run
# tailscaled as a root LaunchDaemon: it is not recovering unattended. The first launch
# asks to allow its network extension.
cask "tailscale-app"

# Kindle. The cask is gone -- Amazon moved distribution to the Mac App Store -- so it comes
# through mas now. Laptop only: it needs an App Store session, and making `make init` on the
# Mac mini depend on one would trade a reading app for a step that can fail during setup.
mas "Kindle", id: 302584613
